# Level 9 → 10

## Goal
Find the password inside `data.txt`, a file containing mostly binary data, on the line preceded by several `=` characters.

## Commands used
```bash
ssh bandit9@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
strings data.txt | grep =
```

## Explanation
`strings` scans a binary/mixed file and extracts only sequences of printable/human-readable text, 
discarding raw binary noise. Piping that into `grep =` narrows the output down to just the line(s) 
containing an `=` character, which is exactly where the password is marked in this file.

